From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: domicile CI <ci@domicile.invalid>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 01:57:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] domicile: an LCD-text re-raster waits for activation

The shell's renderer aborted on a DCHECK in
CanRecreateHighResTilingForLCDTextAndRasterTransform: a sync tree that
loses LCD text to non-opaque contents is never ready to activate. It can
be: an impl-side transform animation that ends after the tree is ready
moves the reason off kTransformAnimation with no commit.

- That branch now waits for the activation, like the check below it.
  The active tree requests an impl-side invalidation, and the next
  pending tree re-rasters without LCD text.

//cc/domicile's DomicileLcdTextActivationTest covers both halves.
---
 cc/layers/picture_layer_impl.cc | 9 ++++++---
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/cc/layers/picture_layer_impl.cc b/cc/layers/picture_layer_impl.cc
index 539d885..83948fc 100644
--- a/cc/layers/picture_layer_impl.cc
+++ b/cc/layers/picture_layer_impl.cc
@@ -1118,9 +1118,12 @@ bool PictureLayerImpl::CanRecreateHighResTilingForLCDTextAndRasterTransform(
     // activate before we have invalidated the existing high rest tiling. This
     // is important to avoid activating a tree with missing tiles which can
     // cause flickering.
-    DCHECK(!layer_tree_impl()->IsSyncTree() ||
-           !layer_tree_impl()->IsReadyToActivate());
-    return true;
+    // DOMICILE: an impl-side transform animation can end after the tree is
+    // ready to activate, which moves the reason here from the animation with
+    // no commit. Wait for the activation, as below; the active tree then asks
+    // for the invalidation that redoes the tiles.
+    return !layer_tree_impl()->IsSyncTree() ||
+           !layer_tree_impl()->IsReadyToActivate();
   }
   // Keep the non-ideal raster translation unchanged for transform animations
   // to avoid re-rasterization during animation.
